  apps/parity/windows-ledger.json                         (page:watch/WatchFace -> done, 2/2)

Data sources (P1/S8 state-holder VM → generated C# client, ADR-004; web hook names kept at the C# call sites):
  useWatchSummary -> WatchFaceSummarySource.StreamAsync, ApiRequest("get_api_v1_watch_summary", vehicle_id=?)
                     parses the full /watch/summary body via WatchFaceSummary.FromResponse
  useWatchCommand -> WatchFaceCommandSender.SendAsync(vehicleId, command),
                     ApiRequest("post_api_v1_watch_command", Body { vehicle_id, command }) — web vehicleId ?? 0
Units (P1/S5): SI read from the API (range_km wire field * 1000 metres; inside_temp_c °C); converted only at the
  display boundary in WatchFaceProjection via UnitFormatters.FormatDistance + UnitConverters.TemperatureFromSi
  ("21°"). No non-SI stored/computed. UnitPref defaults to metric.
Live data: the web page polls via TanStack-Query refetchInterval (30s; no useLiveX/SSE). The native VM exposes
  LoadAsync/RefreshAsync and renders the web "last updated" relative-time caption (WatchFaceProjection.
  FormatRelativeTime) as the freshness indicator (ADR-013).
AI sibling: the opt-in Helix narrator (shared-surfaces/AIWatchFaceNLResponse) is rendered BELOW the OLED face,
  exactly as the web renders <AIWatchFaceNLResponse/> after <WatchShell>. The page's parameterless ctor builds a
  gated-off instance (StaticAiFeatureGate.Off) which collapses itself — preserving the chrome-less wearable
  invariant (web withAiFeature → null).

