        evidence-test: WatchFacePageTests.Loading_model_projects_loading_state,
                       WatchFacePageTests.Manifest_requires_sixteen_string_keys (state-key coverage)
[2/2]  state  success
        WatchFaceState.Success ; WatchFacePageViewModel.LoadAsync -> summary ; WatchFacePage.cs::BuildSuccess
        (vehicle name + battery ring [ChartShapes.ArcPath/ChartGeometry.RingArc tinted by WatchFaceProjection.
        BatteryStatusFor = web getBatteryColor >40/>20] + charging line + TsBadge state [StateStatusFor =
        web watchStateVariant] + 3 tap icons [lock/unlock, climate, sentry] + relative-time caption).
        evidence-test: WatchFacePageTests.Resolved_summary_projects_success_state,
                       WatchFacePageTests.ViewModel_load_populates_success,
                       WatchFacePageTests.Battery_threshold_maps_to_status,
                       WatchFacePageTests.State_badge_variant_matches_web,
                       WatchFacePageTests.Lock_icon_is_dynamic_and_tinted_by_lock_state,
                       WatchFacePageTests.Climate_icon_toggles_command_and_label,
                       WatchFacePageTests.Sentry_icon_is_a_non_interactive_indicator,
                       WatchFacePageTests.Range_converts_from_km_wire_field_at_display_boundary,
                       WatchFacePageTests.Interior_temperature_caption_converts_at_display_boundary,
                       WatchFacePageTests.Charging_line_shows_minutes_to_full_only_when_charging,
                       WatchFacePageTests.Relative_time_matches_web_buckets
# Beyond the 2 required parity states, the web's combined error/empty message branch
#   (`error ? String(error) : 'No vehicle found'`) is implemented as two distinct, never-blank surfaces inside the
#   OLED face — WatchFaceState.Empty (BuildMessage, "No vehicle found") and WatchFaceState.Error (BuildError,
#   localized message + Retry) — so loading/empty/error are all covered for the single data source.
#   evidence-test: No_data_projects_empty_state, ViewModel_empty_body_sets_empty_state,
#                  Failed_model_projects_error_state, ViewModel_load_failure_sets_error_state.
# Command flow (web useWatchCommand): ViewModel_command_sends_then_reloads_summary (re-reads the summary on
#   success, two streams), ViewModel_command_forwards_zero_vehicle_when_no_deep_link, Pending_command_dims_tap_
#   icons_and_spins_active_only. JSON shaping pinned by Summary_parses_full_watch_body / Summary_returns_null_for_
#   non_object_or_empty.
# Strings: all 16 introduced watch.* keys asserted resolved headlessly via a RecordingLocalizer
#   (Projection_resolves_every_required_string_key + Manifest_requires_sixteen_string_keys).
# a11y: AutomationProperties names on the page, the gauge ring, the charging line, the state badge, every tap icon
#   and the retry; the gauge canvas/value/range are AccessibilityView.Raw. The OLED face is `bg-black text-white`
#   per the web wearable EXCEPTION (WatchFacePage.tsx L24) — theme-independent fixed brushes; the value-arc tint
#   (ChartBrushes.ForStatus) and the Helix narrator below still use the W2 design tokens. No charts/maps for this
#   unit (manifest declares 0 charts, 0 maps).

